WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.110
Open Rawaan AI whenever you need help with a question.

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:09.310
In Assistant mode, you can start a general conversation without selecting a client.

3
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:11.789
Type your question and send it.

4
00:00:11.789 --> 00:00:15.389
Earlier conversations are available in Chat history.

5
00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:19.069
Select a client only when you want their records included.

6
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:28.270
For questions about what actually happened in a session, select the client and switch to Records only.

7
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.350
Ask what was documented.

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:35.389
Rawaan shows matching passages from approved notes, with dated source links.

9
00:00:35.389 --> 00:00:38.349
Open the source to check the context.

10
00:00:38.349 --> 00:00:41.469
If there is no relevant record, it says so.

11
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:51.070
Switch back to Assistant for explanations and clinical considerations.

12
00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.190
Suggestions are different from recorded facts.

13
00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:58.669
Confirm current clinical context when Rawaan asks for it.

14
00:00:58.669 --> 00:01:02.029
Web search can bring in references when available.

15
00:01:02.029 --> 00:01:08.349
Check the references and use your own clinical judgment; generated content does not change a saved session note.

16
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.670
A proposed treatment plan is a draft for clinician review.

17
00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:20.270
Choose Review and save plan, read the references, and edit the content.

18
00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:24.429
Use Confirm review and save only after that review.

19
00:01:24.429 --> 00:01:29.229
The saved plan appears in Treatment Plan separately from the original session note.

20
00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:32.349
You remain in control of what enters the record.
